/ save snapshot answers the run's state as a value. Kept in a text file outside the tracked tree (in text a snapshot is
/ its own typed form) and read back as a snapshot in this app, it holds the run's variables and its call stack: the
/ frame this goal runs in comes back, by its goal's address, which only a real snapshot holds.
Start
- set %name% = "Bob"
- save snapshot, write to %snapshot%
- save %snapshot% to 'workspace/saved.txt'
- read file 'workspace/saved.txt', write to %back% as snapshot
- assert %back.actor.list.user.context.variable.name% equals "Bob"
- assert %back.actor.list.user.context.call.root.goal.address% contains "SavesTheRun"
- delete file 'workspace/saved.txt'
